# Miso Chicken and Asparagus
Savory-sweet broiled chicken thighs glazed with a miso-honey marinade and served alongside charred asparagus.

## info
* About 45 minutes
* 4 servings

## ingredients
* 3 tablespoons white miso
* 3 tablespoons mild honey
* 3 tablespoons soy sauce or tamari
* 1 tablespoon rice vinegar
* 2 teaspoons finely grated fresh ginger
* 2 teaspoons finely grated garlic
* 2 teaspoons chile-garlic sauce or other hot sauce
* 1 tablespoon plus 2 teaspoons neutral oil
* 1½ to 2 pounds boneless, skinless chicken thighs
* 1 large bunch asparagus (about 1 pound), trimmed
* Salt and pepper
* 2 scallions, thinly sliced
* Cooked rice (optional), for serving

## steps
1. Make the marinade by whisking together the miso, honey, soy sauce, rice vinegar, ginger, garlic, chile-garlic sauce, 1 tablespoon oil, and 1 tablespoon water in a bowl. Refrigerate half of the marinade for serving.
1. Place the chicken in a shallow dish or zip-top bag and pour the remaining marinade over the chicken. Toss until coated and marinate in the refrigerator for up to 30 minutes.
1. Heat the broiler with a rack positioned about 6 inches below the heating element. Line a large baking sheet with aluminum foil.
1. Remove the chicken from the marinade, scraping off and discarding any excess. Arrange the chicken in a single layer on one side of the baking sheet with the flatter side facing up.
1. Place the asparagus on the other side of the baking sheet. Drizzle with the remaining oil, season with salt and pepper, and toss to coat.
1. Broil until the chicken is cooked through with some charred spots and the asparagus is browned, about 10 minutes.
1. Drizzle the reserved marinade over the chicken and sprinkle with the sliced scallions. Serve with rice if desired.

## notes
* Reserve half of the marinade before it comes into contact with the raw chicken so it can be safely used for serving.
* Do not marinate the chicken longer than 30 minutes, as the miso and salt can affect the texture of the meat.
* Broiler strength varies by oven, so monitor the chicken and asparagus closely during cooking.
* Chicken thighs remain especially juicy under the high heat of the broiler.
